pt09 adversarial lane, surface: gate morphology inflections, upstream of the
gate. Greens the RED frozen in the previous commit.

One word added to the CLAIM_CUES verb list. `date` was the only central verb
of this site's subject matter missing from the step that decides what is a
claim at all — so "Women date up in status." scored 0.16 and was not a claim,
while "Women marry up in status." scored 0.30 and was.

Cost, measured:
- gate floors identical: 191 · 1.0000 · 1.0000 · 0.8529.
- corpus stance census identical: 0 of 1,303 rows move, no score, no label.
  Attributed rather than assumed: 20 corpus units gain claim-likelihood score
  (all already above the threshold), and exactly ONE unit crosses it —
  "Issue date 2016 Jan.", a journal citation header, which the relevance gate
  then bins as non-domain. That is the false positive this buys, frozen in the
  test.
- The class it rescues is short declarative dating sentences, which is forum
  and transcript register. The archive is journalism, whose sentences are long
  enough to clear the threshold on other cues, which is why the corpus cannot
  see this either.

NOT shipped, and recorded as a finding instead: the same line's `marry` still
cannot reach "married" or "marries" — the v2.6.14 trap, alive here too, so
"Women married up in status." remains not claim-like. Fixing it turns
"The merger married two incompatible corporate cultures." claim-like, and that
sentence is the include-override test's deliberate trap (frozen benchmark case
pt-03). Greening that test would mean editing an assertion, so the half that
collides is left for Jason rather than smuggled in beside the half that does
not.

All 18 suite steps green.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 js/lab-analyzer.js | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/js/lab-analyzer.js b/js/lab-analyzer.js
index aedff74..c1dde27 100644
--- a/js/lab-analyzer.js
+++ b/js/lab-analyzer.js
@@ -342,7 +342,7 @@ const CLAIM_CUES = [
   /\b(?:always|never|everyone|nobody|all men|all women|most men|most women)\b/i,
   /\b(?:because|therefore|so that|as a result|the reason)\b/i,
   /\b(?:\d+(?:\.\d+)?\s*%|\b(?:study|studies|research|data|survey|sample)\b)\b/i,
-  /\b(?:prefer|choose|reject|attract|desire|commit|marry|divorce|retain|leave)\w*\b/i,
+  /\b(?:prefer|choose|reject|attract|desire|commit|date|marry|divorce|retain|leave)\w*\b/i,
   /\b(?:meet|make|put|leave|change|matter|narrow|prolong|reward|encourage|discourage|increase|decrease|reduce|delay|shape|affect|influence|sustain|tolerate)\w*\b/i,
 ];
 
